WHY THIS IS NOT PUBLISHED (decision 2026-07-28)
-----------------------------------------------
Lodestone is an internal engine. It is consumed by first-party products
(CodeReckon, RepoPulse) and is deliberately NOT published to any public
package registry. The "private": true flag in package.json is the mechanical
guard against accidental publication; do not remove it without recording a
licensing decision in bpm-market-strategy.

Two reasons publication was rejected rather than licensed restrictively:

1. A restrictive dependency reached through the Apache-2.0 expert system
   would quietly hollow out that project's own licence grant. install.sh
   CLONES github.com/bpmforge/bpm-code-search-mcp publicly, so anything it
   depends on binds every downstream installer — including the consultancies
   the Apache-2.0 grant exists to attract.

2. A licence stops someone selling this code. It does not stop them reading
   it. The retrieval design is the moat; publishing hands that over whatever
   the licence says.

Consequence: bpm-code-search-mcp stays SELF-CONTAINED and must not take a
dependency on this package.
